# project: fraud-ml-migration
VAR train_attempts = 0
VAR labels_sufficient = false
VAR model_beats_rules = false
VAR drift_or_losses = false

-> data_audit

=== data_audit ===
Audit the labeled fraud history: volume, class balance, label quality.
Done when we know whether the labeled set can support training a model.
+ {labels_sufficient} [Labeled history is deep enough] -> train_model
+ {!labels_sufficient} [Labeled history too thin] -> labeling_sprint

=== labeling_sprint ===
Spend a month labeling historical transactions before anything else.
Done when the labeled set reaches the volume and quality the audit called for.
+ [Labeling month complete, dataset ready] -> train_model

=== train_model ===
Train the fraud model and evaluate on the holdout set against the rules engine.
The bar: beat the rules engine on precision AND recall on the holdout.
~ train_attempts += 1
+ {model_beats_rules} [Model beats rules on precision and recall] -> shadow_scoring
+ {train_attempts < 5} [Not there yet, iterate again] ~loop~ -> train_model
+ {train_attempts >= 5} [Several serious attempts, still losing] @human -> keep_rules_writeup

=== keep_rules_writeup ===
Keep the rules engine. Write up why the model could not beat it,
so the next attempt starts from evidence instead of scratch.
+ [Write-up published, project closed] -> END

=== shadow_scoring ===
Shadow-score live traffic for a month: the model runs alongside the rules,
but decisions still come from the rules engine. Collect comparison data.
+ [Shadow month complete, results compiled] -> risk_review

=== risk_review ===
Risk team reviews the shadow month. They own fraud losses,
so the switch is genuinely their call.
+ [Risk team approves the switch] @human -> production_model
+ [Not convinced, more model work first] @human ~loop~ -> train_model
+ [Risk team rejects, keep the rules engine] @human -> keep_rules_writeup

=== production_model ===
Model makes live fraud decisions; auto-retrains weekly.
Monitor data drift alerts and fraud losses against the agreed threshold.
+ {drift_or_losses} [Drift alert or losses above threshold, auto-fallback] -> fallback_to_rules
+ [Model stable long-term, decommission the rules engine] @human -> END

=== fallback_to_rules ===
Automatic fallback: rules engine resumes making decisions immediately.
The whole evaluation starts over from the data audit.
~ train_attempts = 0
~ model_beats_rules = false
~ labels_sufficient = false
~ drift_or_losses = false
+ [Fallback complete, restart evaluation] ~loop~ -> data_audit
